, 2018\nL27@P1: Last Modified: June 13, 2019\nL28@P1: Protocol Integer ID: 15131\nL29@P1: Keywords: cyanobacteria, containing cyanobacterium, prochlorococcus, prochlorococcus marinus, oxyphotobacteria,\nL30@P1: synechococcus, microbiol, first axenic chlorophyll a2, red sea medium medium\nL31@P1: Abstract\nL32@P1: Medium to grow cyanobacteria, in particular Prochlorococcus and Synechococcus\nL33@P1: Reference\nL34@P1: Rippka, R., Coursin, T., Hess, W., Lichtle, C., Scanlan, D.J., Palinska, K.A., Iteman, I. et al. 2000. Prochlorococcus\nL35@P1: marinus Chisholm et al. 1992 subsp. pastoris subsp. nov. strain PCC 9511, the first axenic chlorophyll a2/b2\u0002containing cyanobacterium (Oxyphotobacteria). Int. J. Syst. Evol. Microbiol. 50:183347.\nL36@P1: Guidelines\nL37@P1-2: protocols.io | https://dx.doi.org/10.17504/protocols.io.sz3ef8n June 12, 2019 2/6Materials\nL38@P2: MATERIALS\nL39@P2: Red Sea Salt Red Sea\nL40@P2: STEP MATERIALS\nL41@P2: Red Sea Salt Red Sea\nL42@P2: Protocol materials\nL43@P2: Red Sea Salt Red Sea\nL44@P2: Before start\nL45@P2: Please refer to our general recommendations to grow cultures :\nL46@P2: https://www.protocols.io/private/A48906DC1374AD6281495CB86A8F092F\nL47@P2-3: protocols.io | https://dx.doi.org/10.17504/protocols.io.sz3ef8n June 12, 2019 3/6Prepare solutions\nL48@P3: 1 Hepes-NaOH 1M\nL49@P3: To 250 mL of H20, add gradually 119.15g of Hepes.\nL50@P3: Adjust pH at 7.5 and complete the volume at 500 mL.\nL51@P3: Store in refrigerator.\nL52@P3: 2 Na2-EDTA/FeCl3\nL53@P3: To 40 mL of HCl 0.1 N, add gradually 1,080 g of FeCl3\nL54@P3: To 40 mL of NaOH 0.1 N, add gradually 1,488 g of Na2-EDTA\nL55@P3: Mix both solutions\nL56@P3: Complete final volume to 2 L of sterile water\nL57@P3: Store in refrigerator\nL58@P3: 3 Sodium Phosphate\nL59@P3: Prepare two solutions :\nL60@P3: Monosodium dihydrogen phosphate (NaH2PO4) at 50 mM (6 g in 1 L)\nL61@P3: Disodium hydrogen phosphate (Na2HPo4) at 50 mM (3.55 g in 500 mL)\nL62@P3: Make an equimolar mixture of these two solutions and adjust the pH at 7,5\nL63@P3: 4\nL64@P3: To 500 mL of H20, add gradually elements indicated in the table below.\nL65@P3: Complement the volume to 1L. Store in refrigerator.\nL66@P3: Quan\nL67@P3: tity\nL68@P3: (mg/\nL69@P3: L)\nL70@P3: Merck\nL71@P3: ref. Compound\nL72@P3: Concentr\nL73@P3: ation in\nL74@P3: stock\nL75@P3: solution\nL76@P3: (µM)\nL77@P3: Final\nL78@P3: concentr\nL79@P3: ation in\nL80@P3: medium\nL81@P3: (nM)\nL82@P3: 186 165 Boric acid (H BO ) 3008.25 300.82\nL83@P3: 101 596 Manganese (II) Sulfate Monohydrate\nL84@P3: (MnSO .H O)\nL85@P3: 597.56 59.76\nL86@P3: 1.98 6673 Sodium Tungstate dihydrate\nL87@P3: (Na WO .2H 0)\nL88@P3: 6 0.6\nL89@P3: 5.16 1182 Ammonium molybdate tetrahydrate\nL90@P3: ((NH4)6MO O .4H O)\nL91@P3: 4.18 0.42\nL92@P3: 7.14 4905 Potassium bromide (KBr) 60 6\nL93@P3: 4.98 5043 Potassium iodide (KI) 30 3\nL94@P3: 17.25 8883 Zinc sulfate heptahydrate (ZnSO .7H O) 60 6\nL95@P3: 9.25 2019 Cadium Nitrate (Cd(NO )2.4 O) 30 3\nL96@P3: 3 3\nL97@P3: 4 2\nL98@P3: 2 4 2\nL99@P3: b\nL100@P3: 7 24 2\nL101@P3: 4 2\nL102@P3: 3 H2\nL103@P3-4: protocols.io | https://dx.doi.org/10.17504/protocols.io.sz3ef8n June 12, 2019 4/68.76 2554 Cobalt (II) Nitrate (Co(NO )2.6H O) 30 3\nL104@P4: 7.5 2790 Copper (II) Sulfate (CuSO .5H O) 30 3\nL105@P4: 7.1 6717 Nickel Chloride (NiCl .6H O) 30 3\nL106@P4: 2.4 2481 Chromium (III) Nitrate (Cr(NO )3.9H O) 6 0.6\nL107@P4: 1.5 8503 Vanadyl Sulfate Pentahydrate\nL108@P4: (VOSO .5H O)\nL109@P4: 5.93 0.59\nL110@P4: 28.4 1047 Aluminium Potassium Sulfate\nL111@P4: (KAl(SO4)2.12H O)\nL112@P4: 59.87 5.99\nL113@P4: 3.3 80065\nL114@P4: 3\nL115@P4: Selenium (IV) Oxyde (SeO ) 29.74 2.97\nL116@P4: 3 2\nL117@P4: 4 2\nL118@P4: 2 2\nL119@P4: 3 2\nL120@P4: c\nL121@P4: 4 2\nL122@P4: 2\nL123@P4: 2\nL124@P4: Note\nL125@P4: a -The original receipe uses 300 nM H3BO3 final\nL126@P4: b - 4.94 in the original receipe\nL127@P4: c - 1.52 in the original receipe\nL128@P4: Prepare medium\nL129@P4: 5 We generally prepare two or three 10L carboys at a time\nL130@P4: To 1 L of H2O, add 33.33g of Red Sea Salt\nL131@P4: Dissolve by shaking (20 min on agitator)\nL132@P4: Heat seawater during 20min at 100°C\nL133@P4: Red Sea Salt Red Sea\nL134@P4: 6 Add to seawater under laminar flow hood the following nutriments that have been\nL135@P4: autoclaved (except for vitamin)\nL136@P4: In Roscoff, we generally also add 1 mL NaNO31M for Synechococcus (useless for\nL137@P4: Prochlorococcus but it does not affect the growth)\nL138@P4: Quantit\nL139@P4: y\nL140@P4: Compound Final\nL141@P4: concentration\nL142@P4: 1.0 mL Hepes-NaOH 1M (ph 7,5) - See receipe above 1mM\nL143@P4: 1.0 mL Na2-EDTA/FeCl - See receipe above 2µM\nL144@P4: 1.0 mL Sodium Phosphate (NaPO ) 50mM (pH 7,5) - See\nL145@P4: receipe above\nL146@P4: 50µM\nL147@P4: 3\nL148@P4: a\nL149@P4: 4\nL150@P4-5: protocols.io | https://dx.doi.org/10.17504/protocols.io.sz3ef8n June 12, 2019 5/61.0 mL Ammonium Sulfate 400mM (NH )2-SO 400µM\nL151@P5: 0.1 mL Trace metals “Gaffron+Seˮ - See receipe above\nL152@P5: 0.1 mL\nL153@P5: Cyanocobalamin 10mg/L (Vit. B ) 1µg/L\nL154@P5: 4 4\nL155@P5: b\nL156@P5: 12\nL157@P5: c\nL158@P5: Note\nL159@P5: a - The original recipe is 8 µM (Rippka et al 2000 IJSEM 50, 1833–1847). But it works fine\nL160@P5: for Prochlorococcus...\nL161@P5: b - If one adds 0.1 mL par L, the final concentration of Gaffron in the PCR-S11 medium is\nL162@P5: actually twice more than in the original PCR-S11 recipe.\nL163@P5: c - 10 times less than in the original receipe. Again this seems sufficient...\nL164@P5: 7 Filter the medium on 0.2 micron filter\nL165@P5: protocols.io | https://dx.doi.org/10.17504/protocols.io.sz3ef8n June 12, 2019 6/6\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nChecking your browser - reCAPTCHA (https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2761278/)\nciteturn24view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://pmc.ncb